# Build output.
#
# These are anchored with a leading slash on purpose: an unanchored `porttransit`
# also matches the SOURCE directory cmd/porttransit/, which silently drops the
# command-line entry point from the repository.
/dist/
/porttransit
/porttransit.exe
*.exe

# Local configuration and generated credentials. These hold relay PSKs and the
# console password hash, so they must never be committed.
/config.json
*.local.json

# Logs
*.log

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
# Literal values that must never be published: host addresses, SSH passwords,
# relay PSKs, console password hashes. Read by scripts/check-secrets.sh, which
# is committed while this file is not — so the checker can catch this
# deployment's own values without publishing them in the pattern list.
.secrets-denylist
